00:00:00,010 --> 00:01:33,930
[ Watch on kissFlix.co ]

1
00:02:45,287 --> 00:02:47,667
Why do you try so hard to smile?

2
00:02:49,646 --> 00:02:54,173
Do you put that much effort into everything?

3
00:03:01,828 --> 00:03:03,922
Even when breaking up?

4
00:03:20,170 --> 00:03:23,225
[Episode 23]
[How Lucky There's You, and Us]

5
00:03:25,244 --> 00:03:26,701
Ruan.

6
00:03:26,701 --> 00:03:31,494
We're sending you to your alma mater,
Baidao University, for a presentation.

7
00:03:31,494 --> 00:03:34,400
This is also part of your pre-return duties.

8
00:03:34,400 --> 00:03:36,578
Yes, Manager Wang.

9
00:04:43,413 --> 00:04:45,711
Good. We're here. Let's get out.

10
00:04:47,273 --> 00:04:49,104
- Hello.
- Welcome.

11
00:04:49,104 --> 00:04:50,489
Sorry to keep you waiting.

12
00:04:50,489 --> 00:04:54,000
Not at all. Thanks for coming out in this heat.

13
00:04:54,753 --> 00:04:57,473
- Good. Let's go.
- It's been a while.

14
00:04:58,440 --> 00:05:00,025
Xie Yu!

15
00:05:00,025 --> 00:05:04,857
When I first saw the speaker list,
I wondered if it was the Ruan Si Xian I knew.

16
00:05:04,857 --> 00:05:08,320
But I doubt anyone else has your name.
So I figured it was you.

17
00:05:08,320 --> 00:05:11,040
I didn't recognize you among the students.

18
00:05:11,040 --> 00:05:12,640
I thought you were some kind of student rep.

19
00:05:12,640 --> 00:05:15,920
I wasn't sure it was you
in that uniform either.

20
00:05:15,920 --> 00:05:19,345
How does it feel to be back here?

21
00:05:19,345 --> 00:05:20,510
Nervous.

22
00:05:20,510 --> 00:05:22,080
What are you nervous about?

23
00:05:22,080 --> 00:05:24,865
You can fly a plane.
Surely you can handle this.

24
00:05:24,865 --> 00:05:25,890
That's different.

25
00:05:25,890 --> 00:05:29,200
Then we'll do it the old way.
I'll back you up from below.

26
00:05:29,200 --> 00:05:31,800
Kids these days know so much.

27
00:05:31,800 --> 00:05:33,680
I'm afraid I'll mess up
and be met with total silence.

28
00:05:33,680 --> 00:05:35,160
Then you've got nothing to worry about.

29
00:05:35,160 --> 00:05:39,176
They're all from your own school.
I've already put in a good word for you.

30
00:05:47,035 --> 00:05:48,908
It still tastes the same.

31
00:05:49,816 --> 00:05:52,810
I said I'd treat you to a big meal,
and this is what you picked?

32
00:05:52,810 --> 00:05:56,416
Back in college, this was a big meal.

33
00:05:56,416 --> 00:06:02,301
Back then, every week after the drama club
was over, you'd bring us here to eat.

34
00:06:02,301 --> 00:06:06,846
I remember Nana and I looked forward
to drama club every week.

35
00:06:06,846 --> 00:06:08,231
You weren't just waiting for this meal,
were you?

36
00:06:08,231 --> 00:06:12,836
Of course. This food is what youth tastes like.

37
00:06:12,836 --> 00:06:15,874
You really have changed a lot, Ruan Si Xian.

38
00:06:17,164 --> 00:06:19,857
How's it over there?
Is there a captain with the surname Yue?

39
00:06:19,857 --> 00:06:21,762
You mean Yue Yang?

40
00:06:23,137 --> 00:06:26,119
He's kind of my instructor.

41
00:06:26,119 --> 00:06:29,348
When he was here for the presentation,
he even singled you out and praised you.

42
00:06:29,348 --> 00:06:32,236
He said you improved fast and adapted well.

43
00:06:32,236 --> 00:06:33,725
That's nothing.

44
00:06:33,725 --> 00:06:38,112
I just want to do everything I set out to do.

45
00:06:38,112 --> 00:06:41,729
And about that Hengshi Air Mayday incident,
I saw all of it on the news.

46
00:06:41,729 --> 00:06:45,075
The captain passed out,
and then you hit that brutal thunderstorm.

47
00:06:45,075 --> 00:06:49,040
A hundred-odd lives on that plane were
in your hands. That was really dangerous.

48
00:06:49,040 --> 00:06:54,535
When Hengshi Air 5123 finally landed,
you were basically the pride of our school.

49
00:06:54,535 --> 00:06:56,111
I'm proud of you too.

50
00:06:56,111 --> 00:06:59,331
You even remembered the flight number.

51
00:06:59,331 --> 00:07:03,348
You're still as amazing as ever.
You never forget a thing.

52
00:07:04,378 --> 00:07:06,202
I'm not really amazing.

53
00:07:06,780 --> 00:07:09,416
I just care a little more.

54
00:07:12,686 --> 00:07:16,240
I... I just meant...

55
00:07:16,240 --> 00:07:20,074
Are pilots usually pretty busy at work?

56
00:07:20,074 --> 00:07:22,560
What do you do after work?

57
00:07:22,560 --> 00:07:25,400
We don't do much.

58
00:07:25,400 --> 00:07:29,345
We have dinner, hang out,
then go home to sleep.

59
00:07:29,345 --> 00:07:34,011
I thought you had a wide social circle
and dealt with all kinds of people.

60
00:07:34,011 --> 00:07:35,356
No.

61
00:07:35,356 --> 00:07:37,621
Our circle is actually pretty small.

62
00:07:37,621 --> 00:07:41,432
You're a college professor.
We should be about the same.

63
00:07:42,520 --> 00:07:44,278
So...

64
00:07:47,073 --> 00:07:49,269
Are you seeing anyone now?

65
00:07:54,919 --> 00:07:57,523
- No.
- So...

66
00:07:58,603 --> 00:08:01,182
You don't have the headspace for dating?

67
00:08:02,601 --> 00:08:06,443
Right now, all I care about is flying again.

68
00:08:06,443 --> 00:08:09,397
Nothing else is on my mind.

69
00:08:16,108 --> 00:08:17,108
Ruan.

70
00:08:17,824 --> 00:08:21,019
I've kept up with you all these years.

71
00:08:22,206 --> 00:08:27,116
I regret missing out on someone so wonderful
back when we were in school.

72
00:08:28,194 --> 00:08:29,659
I keep wondering.

73
00:08:29,659 --> 00:08:34,045
You are brilliant, confident, and independent.

74
00:08:34,045 --> 00:08:35,265
But

75
00:08:36,080 --> 00:08:40,842
do you still need someone by your side
to take care of you?

76
00:08:40,842 --> 00:08:44,822
Do you need someone to offer you a shoulder
and be there for you?

77
00:08:46,487 --> 00:08:51,726
I may not be anything special,
but I think at least...

78
00:08:52,822 --> 00:08:56,639
when you're sick, I can buy you medicine.

79
00:08:58,696 --> 00:09:02,981
On your birthday, I can bring you cake.

80
00:09:04,480 --> 00:09:09,059
When you're in danger,
I can protect you, no questions asked.

81
00:09:22,479 --> 00:09:27,685
I don't know
if you'd be willing to give me a chance.

82
00:09:34,280 --> 00:09:35,673
Listen.

83
00:09:36,936 --> 00:09:38,642
I really appreciate it.

84
00:09:38,642 --> 00:09:43,567
But the truth is,
I'm already in love with someone.

85
00:09:50,568 --> 00:09:51,665
I see.

86
00:09:56,167 --> 00:09:57,866
I don't want any regrets.

87
00:09:58,707 --> 00:10:03,564
I don't know
if I could get a chance to catch up.

88
00:10:06,192 --> 00:10:07,660
To be honest,

89
00:10:08,434 --> 00:10:13,600
back in college, I really had feelings for you.

90
00:10:13,600 --> 00:10:18,574
But lately, I've been running from some things.

91
00:10:18,574 --> 00:10:22,901
And it's exactly because of
what you just said to me

92
00:10:23,679 --> 00:10:30,867
that I'm even more certain of
how much I cherish the one I truly love.

93
00:10:33,060 --> 00:10:35,600
I have it figured out now.

94
00:10:35,600 --> 00:10:39,782
The truth is, I can't live without him.

95
00:10:43,061 --> 00:10:45,032
I'm sorry.

96
00:10:46,612 --> 00:10:49,225
Let's move on.

97
00:10:49,225 --> 00:10:50,719
Eat your noodles.

98
00:10:57,479 --> 00:11:00,553
[Together, We'll Meet Above the Clouds]

99
00:11:00,553 --> 00:11:06,358
That's how I became a pilot at Hengshi Air.

100
00:11:06,358 --> 00:11:08,070
Thank you, everyone.

101
00:11:11,792 --> 00:11:14,020
Thank you, Ms. Ruan, for that great speech.

102
00:11:14,020 --> 00:11:15,405
Now we'll open the floor to questions.

103
00:11:15,405 --> 00:11:18,460
Any questions? Please raise your hand.

104
00:11:19,614 --> 00:11:21,224
Yes, you.

105
00:11:21,912 --> 00:11:27,384
Ms. Ruan, how did you feel
the first time you flew a plane solo?

106
00:11:27,384 --> 00:11:33,441
Has anyone here taken the driving test?

107
00:11:34,922 --> 00:11:36,307
Quite a few.

108
00:11:36,307 --> 00:11:41,536
Flying a plane for the first time
is like driving for the first time.

109
00:11:41,536 --> 00:11:43,120
You'll get nervous.

110
00:11:43,120 --> 00:11:46,040
But even more than that, you're excited.

111
00:11:46,040 --> 00:11:50,067
Of course,
flying a plane is, after all, up in the sky.

112
00:11:50,067 --> 00:11:53,000
That feeling just gets amplified.

113
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:56,705
The first time we fly a plane
is called a first solo flight.

114
00:11:56,705 --> 00:11:58,400
It's a milestone.

115
00:11:58,400 --> 00:12:03,385
From then on,
flight students are qualified to fly solo.

116
00:12:03,385 --> 00:12:04,889
It's like getting a driver's license.

117
00:12:04,889 --> 00:12:08,543
When it was my turn, my seniors would pat me
on the shoulder and say,

118
00:12:08,543 --> 00:12:11,879
"Fly well. You've got this.
We'll be waiting for you on the ground."

119
00:12:11,879 --> 00:12:16,960
Such simple words,
but every time I flew, I'd think of them.

120
00:12:16,960 --> 00:12:20,960
Flying itself is easy,
but the journey is amazing.

121
00:12:20,960 --> 00:12:24,424
The first time I flew solo, up in the sky,
I was greedy.

122
00:12:24,424 --> 00:12:26,866
I always felt the flight was too short.

123
00:12:26,866 --> 00:12:30,584
It was like being alone with the one I loved.
There were just the two of us.

124
00:12:30,584 --> 00:12:31,930
I couldn't get enough.

125
00:12:31,930 --> 00:12:35,720
That's when I realized I had fallen
in love with the sky.

126
00:12:35,720 --> 00:12:39,911
And after our first solo flight,
there's always a ritual.

127
00:12:39,911 --> 00:12:41,546
Ice water.

128
00:12:41,546 --> 00:12:43,584
- Ice water?
- Really, ice water?

129
00:12:45,200 --> 00:12:47,664
My seniors didn't spare me either.

130
00:12:47,664 --> 00:12:51,680
A bucket of ice water soaked me head to toe.

131
00:12:51,680 --> 00:12:56,296
So that's what they meant
by waiting for me on the ground.

132
00:12:57,251 --> 00:12:59,916
Then why ice water?

133
00:12:59,916 --> 00:13:02,680
Good question. I asked that too.

134
00:13:02,680 --> 00:13:07,440
My seniors told me it's easy to get a big head
after the first solo flight.

135
00:13:07,440 --> 00:13:10,156
After all, you're up in the sky.

136
00:13:10,800 --> 00:13:16,282
Ice water is a celebration and a reminder

137
00:13:16,282 --> 00:13:21,094
that we should always stay clear-headed,
and never get carried away.

138
00:13:24,560 --> 00:13:26,299
Now I declare

139
00:13:26,299 --> 00:13:31,204
the plan for flight-quality reform
officially approved.

140
00:13:31,204 --> 00:13:36,800
Starting September 30, 2025,
the plan goes into effect.

141
00:13:36,800 --> 00:13:38,070
Great!

142
00:14:09,024 --> 00:14:13,860
I have some good news.
Mr. Fu's reforms got approved!

143
00:14:21,320 --> 00:14:23,998
Come on, share it. Come on.

144
00:14:23,998 --> 00:14:27,120
Like, comment, and post.

145
00:14:27,120 --> 00:14:31,880
The reforms put an end to a 20-year practice
of managing through punishment.

146
00:14:31,880 --> 00:14:36,156
Now we have a healthier and safer environment.
Who wouldn't be excited?

147
00:14:38,777 --> 00:14:40,928
Mr. Fu's reforms got approved!

148
00:14:42,545 --> 00:14:44,911
- That's great!
- That's great!

149
00:14:52,820 --> 00:14:56,745
Let's give this young lady a chance. Go ahead.

150
00:14:56,745 --> 00:14:57,870
Thank you.

151
00:14:57,870 --> 00:14:59,495
I'd like to ask Ms. Ruan a question.

152
00:14:59,495 --> 00:15:02,439
What advantages do women have
when learning to fly?

153
00:15:02,439 --> 00:15:04,056
Women don't have any advantages.

154
00:15:04,056 --> 00:15:07,225
Not only do women not have any,
men don't, either.

155
00:15:07,225 --> 00:15:10,689
When it comes to flying,
there may be some personal advantages.

156
00:15:10,689 --> 00:15:15,625
For example, academically strong students
may find the theory classes a little easier.

157
00:15:15,625 --> 00:15:18,890
But in flight training,
you can't rely on those advantages.

158
00:15:18,890 --> 00:15:24,360
We have to set aside everything we're proud of
and stay grounded and humble.

159
00:15:24,360 --> 00:15:28,704
After all, flying is about safety.
There is no room for arrogance.

160
00:15:28,704 --> 00:15:30,358
Thank you.

161
00:15:32,971 --> 00:15:35,400
Ms. Ruan.
I've been following you for a long time.

162
00:15:35,400 --> 00:15:37,680
You have a lot of followers online.

163
00:15:37,680 --> 00:15:41,560
You get mostly comments like
"beautiful," "handsome," and "gorgeous pilot."

164
00:15:41,560 --> 00:15:45,357
But as far as I know,
airlines spend a lot of money training pilots.

165
00:15:45,357 --> 00:15:47,504
So they're very cautious
about hiring female pilots.

166
00:15:47,504 --> 00:15:53,474
Do you think you got your offer
because of your skills, or your looks?

167
00:16:01,598 --> 00:16:04,772
- Why is this guy talking like that?
- Yeah. That's so out of line.

168
00:16:04,772 --> 00:16:06,339
What's going on?

169
00:16:06,339 --> 00:16:09,096
<i>That really is a mixed bag of a question.</i>

170
00:16:10,226 --> 00:16:11,454
First,

171
00:16:11,454 --> 00:16:14,692
I'm very grateful
for everyone's compliments about my looks.

172
00:16:14,692 --> 00:16:19,193
But honestly, I haven't done much to earn that.

173
00:16:19,193 --> 00:16:25,670
What I have worked hardest on is flying.

174
00:16:30,151 --> 00:16:32,058
It really wasn't easy.

175
00:16:32,058 --> 00:16:35,844
Any other questions out there?

176
00:16:35,844 --> 00:16:37,313
Okay, you there.

177
00:16:37,313 --> 00:16:39,252
Ms. Ruan, I have a question.

178
00:16:39,252 --> 00:16:43,519
Pilots work such exhausting hours,
and the pressure is intense.

179
00:16:43,519 --> 00:16:45,823
So I'd like to know if you're married.

180
00:16:45,823 --> 00:16:51,561
And I'd also like to ask
how female pilots balance work and family?

181
00:16:51,561 --> 00:16:53,387
I can tell you're single.

182
00:16:53,387 --> 00:16:55,840
You haven't been through the wringer
of love yet.

183
00:16:55,840 --> 00:16:57,145
I'm single too.

184
00:16:57,145 --> 00:16:59,880
So I don't have to balance work and family.

185
00:16:59,880 --> 00:17:02,960
If this were the old me,
I might have asked you back.

186
00:17:02,960 --> 00:17:08,203
"Why not ask male pilots
how they balance work and family?"

187
00:17:11,059 --> 00:17:14,998
But today,
I actually want to share something with you.

188
00:17:14,998 --> 00:17:19,751
It's about a female captain
and how she balances work and family.

189
00:17:21,636 --> 00:17:24,178
<i>This female captain was my flight instructor.</i>

190
00:17:24,178 --> 00:17:27,124
<i>There are promotion requirements for us pilots.</i>

191
00:17:27,124 --> 00:17:31,156
<i>To become a first officer,
you need 300 flight hours.</i>

192
00:17:31,156 --> 00:17:34,464
<i>Then, you need 3,000 flight hours</i>

193
00:17:34,464 --> 00:17:37,644
<i>before you're eligible
for the captain's promotion exam.</i>

194
00:17:38,418 --> 00:17:41,683
<i>After becoming captain,
you must safely log another 3,000 hours.</i>

195
00:17:41,683 --> 00:17:44,149
<i>Then you can take the instructor exam.</i>

196
00:17:44,149 --> 00:17:49,440
So she already has years of flying experience.

197
00:17:49,440 --> 00:17:51,985
Her spouse is also a captain.

198
00:17:51,985 --> 00:17:55,774
In our industry,
we call that a dual-pilot family.

199
00:17:56,559 --> 00:18:01,923
They have a very cute daughter in kindergarten.

200
00:18:01,923 --> 00:18:08,156
<i>Usually, one of them will leave work to care
for the family full-time.</i>

201
00:18:08,876 --> 00:18:12,859
<i>Most of the time, it's the woman who does it.</i>

202
00:18:12,859 --> 00:18:14,249
<i>But she didn't.</i>

203
00:18:14,249 --> 00:18:16,986
<i>She sent her child to full-time daycare.</i>

204
00:18:16,986 --> 00:18:21,465
She only brings the girl home to spend time
with her when she's off.

205
00:18:21,465 --> 00:18:22,893
She told me that

206
00:18:22,893 --> 00:18:26,938
when she's worn out from flying,
she'll skip picking up her child sometimes.

207
00:18:27,657 --> 00:18:31,658
Because only when she's well-rested

208
00:18:31,658 --> 00:18:35,729
can she show up at her best for her flights.

209
00:18:35,729 --> 00:18:38,194
<i>So is there balance?</i>

210
00:18:38,194 --> 00:18:41,433
<i>Maybe a little.</i>

211
00:18:41,433 --> 00:18:44,626
<i>But more than that, it's about sacrifice.</i>

212
00:18:44,626 --> 00:18:47,532
It's actually the same for everyone
with work and school.

213
00:18:47,532 --> 00:18:49,391
If you're preparing for grad school
or the civil service exam,

214
00:18:49,391 --> 00:18:54,457
you have to give up some leisure and rest time.

215
00:18:54,457 --> 00:19:00,762
And she put most of her energy
into her flying career.

216
00:19:00,762 --> 00:19:03,666
I remember my mentor once told me this.

217
00:19:03,666 --> 00:19:07,092
She said, "Si Xian, do you know?

218
00:19:08,120 --> 00:19:14,520
We should treat the passengers behind us
as our elders and siblings.

219
00:19:14,520 --> 00:19:18,435
This flight might take them to family,

220
00:19:18,435 --> 00:19:22,214
<i>to friends, to dreams, and to love.</i>

221
00:19:22,214 --> 00:19:26,280
We have to get every passenger safely
to their destination.

222
00:19:26,280 --> 00:19:30,810
This is our highest calling as pilots."

223
00:19:44,400 --> 00:19:47,559
Go ahead. Everyone. Come on.

224
00:19:49,457 --> 00:19:50,643
- You've all worked hard.
- Thank you.

225
00:19:50,643 --> 00:19:52,348
You've been working hard.

226
00:19:52,348 --> 00:19:54,640
Let's save the formalities. Mr. Yu.

227
00:19:54,640 --> 00:19:57,319
You've all worked hard. I'd like to
thank all of you for your support and trust.

228
00:19:57,319 --> 00:19:59,380
Come on.

229
00:19:59,380 --> 00:20:00,413
Keep it up.

230
00:20:00,413 --> 00:20:01,759
- Thank you.
- I'll head over there first.

231
00:20:01,759 --> 00:20:03,418
- Okay. Go ahead.
- Okay.

232
00:20:04,563 --> 00:20:08,440
- I won't be drinking tonight.
- Thanks for all your hard work.

233
00:20:08,440 --> 00:20:10,104
- Sure. Okay.
- Come on.

234
00:20:10,104 --> 00:20:11,284
Sure.

235
00:20:13,200 --> 00:20:15,394
Okay. Excuse us for a moment.

236
00:20:20,969 --> 00:20:25,291
You think you're so capable?

237
00:20:26,529 --> 00:20:27,852
No.

238
00:20:28,698 --> 00:20:31,846
I'm only doing this to keep up with the times.

239
00:20:31,846 --> 00:20:33,983
That's where things are headed.

240
00:20:33,983 --> 00:20:36,290
Don't you think the cost is a bit high?

241
00:20:36,290 --> 00:20:37,290
Dad.

242
00:20:38,072 --> 00:20:42,042
Do you remember what I said a few years ago?

243
00:20:42,042 --> 00:20:47,836
Reform would inevitably bring pain
and also sacrifice.

244
00:20:49,083 --> 00:20:52,531
If I have to pay that price,

245
00:20:52,531 --> 00:20:58,824
and if paying that price leads to
a better future for Hengshi, I'm willing.

246
00:21:02,395 --> 00:21:04,048
Ming Yu.

247
00:21:05,554 --> 00:21:10,049
You used to try so hard to look the part.

248
00:21:10,906 --> 00:21:14,772
But now, you really have changed.

249
00:21:14,772 --> 00:21:19,904
Back then, you cut staff
and scrapped the Soar Initiative.

250
00:21:21,137 --> 00:21:27,843
To the other board members and me,
all those seemed a bit immature.

251
00:21:27,843 --> 00:21:31,280
They even seemed a little arrogant.

252
00:21:31,280 --> 00:21:37,634
But I just like that drive of yours.

253
00:21:37,634 --> 00:21:43,898
Actually, I've been wanting
to tell you this for a while.

254
00:21:43,898 --> 00:21:45,910
I'm getting old.

255
00:21:47,043 --> 00:21:51,427
The men who made their way in the world
with me are getting old too.

256
00:21:51,427 --> 00:21:52,573
From here on out,

257
00:21:52,573 --> 00:21:58,738
whether it's Hengshi Air
or the aviation industry as a whole,

258
00:22:00,153 --> 00:22:03,422
it'll all depend on young people like you.

259
00:22:07,673 --> 00:22:11,909
There's something I need to say,
and you can't let it go to your head.

260
00:22:13,944 --> 00:22:18,327
When you joined Hengshi after coming back home,

261
00:22:19,360 --> 00:22:21,425
I had a lot of faith in you.

262
00:22:21,425 --> 00:22:23,906
And now,

263
00:22:23,906 --> 00:22:28,520
you really have done everything I hoped for.

264
00:22:28,520 --> 00:22:30,232
So,

265
00:22:31,880 --> 00:22:34,934
I've believed in you all along.

266
00:22:37,818 --> 00:22:39,890
I knew you could do it.

267
00:22:44,378 --> 00:22:46,077
- Mr. Fu.
- Hello.

268
00:22:48,486 --> 00:22:50,353
Congratulations on the reforms.

269
00:22:50,353 --> 00:22:51,787
You've worked hard.

270
00:22:52,789 --> 00:22:54,656
I've been watching this stream for a while.

271
00:22:54,656 --> 00:22:56,883
I think you'd be more interested than I am.

272
00:22:56,883 --> 00:23:02,057
<i>Actually, for some reason,
I'm currently grounded.</i>

273
00:23:03,312 --> 00:23:08,480
<i>At first, I was calm about being grounded.</i>

274
00:23:08,480 --> 00:23:11,144
<i>I accept all of life's twists and turns.</i>

275
00:23:11,144 --> 00:23:15,489
<i>Because before that,
I'd already been through far more upheaval.</i>

276
00:23:15,489 --> 00:23:19,943
I had more time for myself
after being grounded.

277
00:23:19,943 --> 00:23:24,648
Then one day, a plane flew over my head.

278
00:23:24,648 --> 00:23:30,608
That was when I realized
I had drifted so far from flying.

279
00:23:30,608 --> 00:23:35,365
That was when I realized
how deeply my heart longed for flight.

280
00:23:35,365 --> 00:23:40,379
I started to miss my days at flight school
practicing day and night.

281
00:23:40,379 --> 00:23:45,372
I missed the wild water celebration
after my first solo.

282
00:23:45,372 --> 00:23:47,797
I missed the rush of my first flight.

283
00:23:47,797 --> 00:23:51,537
I missed the heat I felt every time I flew.

284
00:23:51,537 --> 00:23:53,419
It was like...

285
00:23:54,797 --> 00:23:56,965
you were in love with someone.

286
00:23:57,960 --> 00:24:02,800
But then the two of you,
for one reason or another,

287
00:24:02,800 --> 00:24:04,800
had to be apart for a while.

288
00:24:04,800 --> 00:24:08,753
<i>You miss many things you've grown used to.</i>

289
00:24:08,753 --> 00:24:13,762
<i>Late at night, you think back to life with him.</i>

290
00:24:13,762 --> 00:24:19,680
You remember the wind he brought
when you two met.

291
00:24:19,680 --> 00:24:21,360
Now and then,

292
00:24:21,360 --> 00:24:23,412
in your dreams,

293
00:24:24,292 --> 00:24:25,867
he would still show up.

294
00:24:25,867 --> 00:24:29,640
<i>When you wake up, you feel a pang of loss.</i>

295
00:24:29,640 --> 00:24:35,992
<i>So you realize you miss
those happy and memorable moments.</i>

296
00:24:36,820 --> 00:24:42,488
Even those unhappy moments
will make you miss them.

297
00:24:43,928 --> 00:24:45,327
Because...

298
00:24:47,114 --> 00:24:49,067
they're gone for good.

299
00:24:49,067 --> 00:24:50,698
<i>So I admit</i>

300
00:24:51,960 --> 00:24:57,010
<i>I treasure the time I spent with him.</i>

301
00:24:57,720 --> 00:24:59,040
Where are they performing?

302
00:24:59,040 --> 00:25:00,240
Where? Tell him now.

303
00:25:00,240 --> 00:25:02,906
Mr. Fu, I've already sent you the address.

304
00:25:02,906 --> 00:25:04,290
Nice work.

305
00:25:06,197 --> 00:25:13,680
For me, flying is like
meeting the one I'm so eager to see.

306
00:25:13,680 --> 00:25:17,461
I believe you'll also be willing
to fight for dreams.

307
00:25:17,461 --> 00:25:20,160
You'll keep moving toward your future.

308
00:25:20,160 --> 00:25:25,186
Put faith
in the right person and the right thing.

309
00:25:25,186 --> 00:25:29,084
They will always be waiting
for you at the finish line.

310
00:26:27,160 --> 00:26:32,760
[Moment]

311
00:26:32,760 --> 00:26:38,452
How did you manage
to spit out that much flattery?

312
00:26:46,012 --> 00:26:48,965
[My Moment]
[Posted]

313
00:26:54,714 --> 00:27:00,686
With news this good,
shouldn't I celebrate with a meal?

314
00:27:02,360 --> 00:27:05,514
That place should still be open.

315
00:28:05,864 --> 00:28:06,920
[Ocean Fresh Clam Noodles]
Bye.

316
00:28:06,920 --> 00:28:09,004
- Take care.
- Goodbye.

317
00:28:11,480 --> 00:28:12,553
- Excuse me.
- Yes?

318
00:28:12,553 --> 00:28:14,193
A clam noodle, please.

319
00:28:16,080 --> 00:28:18,745
You look familiar.
I haven't seen you in years, have I?

320
00:28:18,745 --> 00:28:22,040
Yeah. I graduated years ago.
And you still remember me?

321
00:28:22,040 --> 00:28:25,224
Of course I do.
Well, do you still take the original flavor?

322
00:28:25,224 --> 00:28:26,610
Yes. I'll take one.

323
00:28:26,610 --> 00:28:29,141
- Have a seat. It'll be right out.
- Okay.

324
00:28:50,906 --> 00:28:52,332
- Excuse me.
- Yes?

325
00:28:52,332 --> 00:28:54,844
- One clam noodle, please. Thanks.
- Okay.

326
00:29:01,227 --> 00:29:03,207
What are you doing here?

327
00:29:03,207 --> 00:29:05,103
I'm here to collect a debt.

328
00:29:07,297 --> 00:29:10,464
Collect what? What debt?

329
00:29:10,464 --> 00:29:14,696
You'd better keep your word.

330
00:29:15,780 --> 00:29:18,845
My word?

331
00:29:18,845 --> 00:29:21,121
You said you'd love me forever.

332
00:29:21,970 --> 00:29:24,240
You said you'd always stay with me.

333
00:29:24,240 --> 00:29:25,424
Dream on!

334
00:29:25,424 --> 00:29:30,310
Have you been overworked lately?
You're talking nonsense.

335
00:29:38,232 --> 00:29:39,952
Did you post this?

336
00:29:41,113 --> 00:29:43,546
I did. What's wrong?

337
00:29:43,546 --> 00:29:45,617
Take another close look.

338
00:29:47,674 --> 00:29:48,925
The last line.

339
00:29:49,585 --> 00:29:52,299
You said,
"Mr. Fu, you worked hard. Love you forever.

340
00:29:52,299 --> 00:29:54,391
I will stay with you forever."

341
00:29:58,093 --> 00:30:02,680
I... That was a repost. I copied and pasted.

342
00:30:02,680 --> 00:30:04,811
I don't care how it happened.
I only care about the result.

343
00:30:04,811 --> 00:30:06,275
That's a confession.

344
00:30:06,275 --> 00:30:09,116
Then by that logic, my mentor reposted it too.

345
00:30:09,116 --> 00:30:11,880
How's that?
You want to come between a married couple?

346
00:30:11,880 --> 00:30:13,880
I don't care what anyone else posts.

347
00:30:15,050 --> 00:30:17,108
I only care about what you post.

348
00:30:21,284 --> 00:30:24,360
Then I'll delete it right now.

349
00:30:24,360 --> 00:30:26,044
Don't you dare!

350
00:31:22,220 --> 00:31:23,737
Tomorrow.

351
00:31:25,726 --> 00:31:28,034
Tomorrow I'll give you a surprise.

352
00:31:50,342 --> 00:31:51,962
Oh my God.

353
00:32:09,134 --> 00:32:12,320
Honey. I was wrong. I was wrong!

354
00:32:12,320 --> 00:32:15,040
- What did you do wrong?
- Well.

355
00:32:15,040 --> 00:32:17,625
I shouldn't have eaten the cake you bought
in one bite.

356
00:32:17,625 --> 00:32:19,280
From now on,
I'll save all the good stuff for you.

357
00:32:19,280 --> 00:32:22,985
- Anything else?
- I really don't know.

358
00:32:22,985 --> 00:32:25,211
Next time you mess up, just apologize.

359
00:32:25,211 --> 00:32:27,795
If kissing worked, why would anyone go to war?

360
00:32:27,795 --> 00:32:31,501
Stop copying those stupid guys, okay?

361
00:32:31,501 --> 00:32:34,815
<i>The only thing you need to do is kiss her.</i>

362
00:32:34,815 --> 00:32:37,411
<i>Kiss her like you mean it. Kiss her like crazy.
Kiss her, and you're done.</i>

363
00:32:37,411 --> 00:32:41,477
<i>Only after you kiss her will you understand
that girls love that.</i>

364
00:32:41,477 --> 00:32:43,948
Honey, I really was wrong.

365
00:33:09,784 --> 00:33:11,470
Time to get out.

366
00:33:13,503 --> 00:33:15,189
Careful.

367
00:33:16,640 --> 00:33:18,265
What are you up to?

368
00:33:18,265 --> 00:33:19,891
- Why make it so--
- Mysterious?

369
00:33:19,891 --> 00:33:21,876
Over the top.

370
00:33:21,876 --> 00:33:23,573
Over the top?

371
00:33:23,573 --> 00:33:26,397
If you find it over the top after seeing it,

372
00:33:27,185 --> 00:33:28,651
you can say no.

373
00:33:28,651 --> 00:33:29,911
No way.

374
00:33:30,818 --> 00:33:32,355
Ready?

375
00:34:04,106 --> 00:34:05,936
Oh...

376
00:34:05,936 --> 00:34:09,604
Fu Ming Yu, what is this?

377
00:34:10,920 --> 00:34:13,165
Just what it looks like.

378
00:34:14,160 --> 00:34:15,880
I registered it for you.

379
00:34:15,880 --> 00:34:18,866
From now on, you can fly whenever you want to.

380
00:34:18,866 --> 00:34:21,440
This is seriously over the top.

381
00:34:21,440 --> 00:34:26,240
So, Captain Ruan,
do you want to take it for a test flight?

382
00:34:28,940 --> 00:34:30,486
Right now?

383
00:34:32,665 --> 00:34:33,863
Go on.

384
00:34:49,080 --> 00:34:52,185
I can fly today? Did you file the flight plan?

385
00:34:52,185 --> 00:34:55,040
I did. Your license hasn't expired, has it?

386
00:34:55,040 --> 00:34:57,320
Of course not.

387
00:34:57,320 --> 00:34:58,574
Get in.

388
00:35:01,121 --> 00:35:02,387
I'm not going up.

389
00:35:02,387 --> 00:35:04,981
This is your solo flight. You got this.

390
00:35:05,827 --> 00:35:10,535
If you don't get in, then I'm not flying today.

391
00:35:12,746 --> 00:35:14,010
Tower, good afternoon.

392
00:35:14,010 --> 00:35:17,600
<i>Bravo-12 Tango Juliet, ready.
Requesting taxi clearance.</i>

393
00:35:17,600 --> 00:35:19,800
<i>Bravo-12 Tango Juliet, cleared to taxi.</i>

394
00:35:19,800 --> 00:35:23,360
<i>Hold short of Runway 17 at A-A1.</i>

395
00:35:23,360 --> 00:35:28,476
<i>Hold short of Runway 17 at A-A1.
Bravo-12 Tango Juliet.</i>

396
00:35:37,738 --> 00:35:41,058
<i>Bravo-12 Tango Juliet, taxi onto Runway 17.</i>

397
00:35:41,058 --> 00:35:44,539
<i>Taxi onto Runway 17. Bravo-12 Tango Juliet.</i>

398
00:35:50,651 --> 00:35:54,921
<i>Tower, Bravo-12 Tango Juliet ready
for takeoff clearance.</i>

399
00:35:54,921 --> 00:35:58,420
Bravo-12 Tango Juliet.
<i>Surface wind 170 at 2 meters per second.</i>

400
00:35:58,420 --> 00:36:00,645
<i>Runway 17 cleared for takeoff.</i>

401
00:36:00,645 --> 00:36:04,320
<i>Runway 17 cleared for takeoff.
Bravo-12 Tango Juliet.</i>

402
00:36:04,320 --> 00:36:08,586
<i>Mr. Fu, hold on. We're taking off.</i>

403
00:36:08,586 --> 00:36:09,842
Okay.

404
00:36:38,715 --> 00:36:41,400
<i>- You're not asleep, are you?
- No.</i>

405
00:36:42,541 --> 00:36:47,486
<i>Your eyes are closed. Open them.
It's beautiful out there.</i>

406
00:36:48,406 --> 00:36:53,800
<i>Look ahead. That cloud is a thundercloud.
It looks amazing.</i>

407
00:36:53,800 --> 00:36:58,825
<i>Yes, it is. Can we stop looking at the clouds?</i>

408
00:36:58,825 --> 00:37:01,647
<i>Focus.</i>

409
00:37:11,307 --> 00:37:12,652
<i>To be honest,</i>

410
00:37:12,652 --> 00:37:17,757
<i>those grounded days were really frustrating.</i>

411
00:37:17,757 --> 00:37:21,981
<i>I kept thinking about flight school.</i>

412
00:37:21,981 --> 00:37:24,557
<i>Especially my first solo.</i>

413
00:37:24,557 --> 00:37:26,353
<i>It was so amazing.</i>

414
00:37:30,691 --> 00:37:34,106
<i>Open your eyes. It's really beautiful outside.</i>

415
00:37:45,282 --> 00:37:46,892
<i>Pretty nice, right?</i>

416
00:37:59,004 --> 00:38:00,550
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

417
00:38:01,385 --> 00:38:03,770
<i>The flight ban must have been hard on you.</i>

418
00:38:06,993 --> 00:38:08,960
<i>It's not that bad.</i>

419
00:38:08,960 --> 00:38:13,958
<i>The break actually made me more determined
to follow what I want.</i>

420
00:38:15,129 --> 00:38:17,401
<i>I want to fly.</i>

421
00:38:17,401 --> 00:38:19,715
<i>I need to love and be loved.</i>

422
00:38:19,715 --> 00:38:21,331
<i>I need you.</i>

423
00:38:29,137 --> 00:38:30,559
<i>Your heart rate is too fast.</i>

424
00:38:30,559 --> 00:38:33,566
<i>May I ask if you need me to call for help?</i>

425
00:38:38,333 --> 00:38:39,446
<i>Mr. Fu.</i>

426
00:38:40,359 --> 00:38:42,436
<i>Am I going too fast?</i>

427
00:38:43,440 --> 00:38:44,440
<i>No.</i>

428
00:38:46,440 --> 00:38:49,126
<i>You changed your tune too fast.</i>

429
00:38:53,731 --> 00:38:56,978
<i>I've kept a secret from you.</i>

430
00:38:58,764 --> 00:39:00,519
<i>I actually took flight lessons before.</i>

431
00:39:00,519 --> 00:39:03,159
<i>You did? You already know how to fly.</i>

432
00:39:03,159 --> 00:39:07,344
<i>Fear comes from not trusting yourself.</i>

433
00:39:07,344 --> 00:39:11,569
<i>You can distrust anyone,
but you have to trust yourself.</i>

434
00:39:15,760 --> 00:39:18,464
<i>Those wings are yours.</i>

435
00:39:18,464 --> 00:39:21,285
<i>Feel the flight. Feel the wind.</i>

436
00:39:22,134 --> 00:39:23,882
<i>You have to believe in yourself.</i>

437
00:39:23,882 --> 00:39:26,086
<i>Don't be scared. I've got you.</i>

438
00:39:27,269 --> 00:39:28,940
<i>This sunset is gorgeous.</i>

439
00:39:28,940 --> 00:39:33,886
<i>Years from now,
you'll still say it's beautiful.</i>

440
00:39:33,886 --> 00:39:37,349
<i>We're chasing the sunset again, aren't we?</i>

441
00:39:37,349 --> 00:39:40,165
<i>As long as you don't leave me halfway.</i>

442
00:39:40,165 --> 00:39:42,804
<i>Why are you still holding a grudge?</i>

443
00:39:42,804 --> 00:39:44,680
<i>So petty.</i>

444
00:39:44,680 --> 00:39:50,278
<i>Yeah. I can't forget it.</i>

445
00:39:50,278 --> 00:39:52,469
<i>I can't forget that helpless feeling.</i>

446
00:39:53,646 --> 00:39:56,993
<i>I also can't forget that I left you
in such a helpless situation.</i>

447
00:39:58,650 --> 00:40:00,442
<i>Promise me.</i>

448
00:40:00,442 --> 00:40:03,188
<i>Next time, don't
walk away on your own like that.</i>

449
00:40:03,188 --> 00:40:08,250
<i>Remember, hard times will always be there,
whether you're by my side or not.</i>

450
00:40:09,070 --> 00:40:10,684
<i>But if you're not by my side--</i>

451
00:40:10,684 --> 00:40:15,042
<i>When I'm not there, you can really shine.</i>

452
00:40:15,042 --> 00:40:18,632
<i>Otherwise, how can reform move forward, right?</i>

453
00:40:22,890 --> 00:40:26,541
<i>Let me show you something exciting.</i>

454
00:40:45,275 --> 00:40:49,459
When you were doing that stunt,
you forgot you'd have to drive back, right?

455
00:40:49,459 --> 00:40:51,331
But it's fine.

456
00:40:51,331 --> 00:40:56,555
You can even fly a plane.
A tiny little car is nothing.

457
00:40:56,555 --> 00:40:59,861
It's not that I don't trust my own skills.

458
00:40:59,861 --> 00:41:01,996
I just can't afford to wreck your car.

459
00:41:01,996 --> 00:41:04,459
I was the only one in the airspace.

460
00:41:04,459 --> 00:41:06,600
I could fly however I wanted.

461
00:41:06,600 --> 00:41:09,120
The sky's not like the road.

462
00:41:09,120 --> 00:41:14,149
I'm just afraid that, once you start driving,
you'll say it's too slow.

463
00:41:15,480 --> 00:41:18,505
Okay, that's enough coming from you.

464
00:41:18,505 --> 00:41:20,494
- Hold on tight.
- Wait!

465
00:41:29,087 --> 00:41:30,906
Ruan Si Xian!

466
00:41:36,107 --> 00:41:39,000
- Hello.
<i>- Mr. Fu, your father's already pressing us.</i>

467
00:41:39,000 --> 00:41:41,920
<i>We need to head to Ma'ao soon.
When do you want to set off?</i>

468
00:41:41,920 --> 00:41:44,859
I'll tell you later. I have to go.

469
00:41:46,441 --> 00:41:48,225
A business trip?

470
00:41:49,773 --> 00:41:51,426
I'll be stationed there.

471
00:41:52,584 --> 00:41:56,956
<i>A few years ago,
you went to Ma'ao's W.T. Airport.</i>

472
00:41:56,956 --> 00:42:02,604
<i>To be honest, since Hengshi Air acquired it,
it hasn't made a dime.</i>

473
00:42:02,604 --> 00:42:05,230
<i>Your reforms made a huge splash.</i>

474
00:42:05,230 --> 00:42:07,215
<i>Looks like you won.</i>

475
00:42:07,215 --> 00:42:10,493
<i>But you know a lot of the board is unhappy.</i>

476
00:42:10,493 --> 00:42:14,514
<i>I have to prove to them how capable you are.</i>

477
00:42:14,514 --> 00:42:18,740
<i>So from here on, W.T. Airport is yours.</i>

478
00:42:18,740 --> 00:42:23,386
<i>You have one year to turn it around.</i>

479
00:42:23,386 --> 00:42:25,453
Then you're going to Ma'ao?

480
00:42:25,453 --> 00:42:28,300
You don't really have to go
for a whole year, do you?

481
00:42:28,300 --> 00:42:29,590
What?

482
00:42:30,324 --> 00:42:33,190
You're not scheming to leave me again, are you?

483
00:42:33,190 --> 00:42:35,148
Of course not.

484
00:42:35,983 --> 00:42:38,891
I thought they were forcing me out.

485
00:42:38,891 --> 00:42:41,812
I didn't expect them to force you out.

486
00:42:41,812 --> 00:42:44,101
So you turn out to be a burden.

487
00:42:44,101 --> 00:42:46,933
Just tell me
if I was wise to leave you back then.

488
00:42:47,680 --> 00:42:51,389
How can someone fall into the same trap twice?

489
00:42:51,389 --> 00:42:53,360
Me? A trap?

490
00:42:53,360 --> 00:42:56,000
Just tell me if I ended up with a fake tycoon.

491
00:42:56,000 --> 00:42:59,529
How come I get no special treatment?
I just keep getting the short end of the stick.

492
00:42:59,529 --> 00:43:00,795
Ruan Si Xian.

493
00:43:00,795 --> 00:43:03,297
It's too late to say that now.

494
00:43:03,297 --> 00:43:05,804
Why don't you quit? I'll take care of you.

495
00:43:05,804 --> 00:43:08,920
So you don't want me to go to Ma'ao?

496
00:43:08,920 --> 00:43:10,120
You can't bear to let me go?

497
00:43:10,120 --> 00:43:13,960
I just can't stand the thought
of you enjoying the good life on your own.

